     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I would like to build up a tiny shiny application to interpolate spatial data. My scenario is like this: <br>1. The user is able to upload a CSV file (that contains the variable and coordination information). <br>2.  The user can choose a specific column (variable) from an updated list. <br>3. The shiny app (server part) do the interpolation and other analysis with this variable.  <br><br>I have borrowed some useful codes and is able to update the list of column. However, gstat function (<a href=\"http://gstat.cv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://gstat.cv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792390011790000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0EzhQa3TCAlN4PD7079b20\">gstat.cv</a>) does not work properly.  <br><br>Here is the code for UI: <br><br>library(shiny)<br>ui &lt;- fluidPage(<br>  h2(&#39;The uploaded file data&#39;),<br>  dataTableOutput(&#39;mytable&#39;),<br>  fileInput(&#39;file&#39;, &#39;Choose info-file to upload&#39;,<br>            accept = c(<br>              &#39;text/csv&#39;,<br>              &#39;text/comma-separated-values&#39;,<br>              &#39;text/tab-separated-values&#39;,<br>              &#39;text/plain&#39;,<br>              &#39;.csv&#39;,<br>              &#39;.tsv&#39;<br>            )<br>  ),<br>  <br>  actionButton(&quot;choice&quot;, &quot;Choose column to optimize&quot;),<br>  <br>  selectInput(&quot;columns&quot;, &quot;Select Columns&quot;, choices = NULL),<br>  <br>  tableOutput(&quot;table_display&quot;)<br>)<br><br>and here is part of the code for the server: <br><br>server &lt;- function(input, output, session) { # added session for updateSelectInput<br>  <br>  library(gstat)<br>  library(sp)<br>  <br>  dulieu &lt;- eventReactive(input$choice, {<br>    inFile &lt;- input$file<br>    # Instead # if (is.null(inFile)) ... use &quot;req&quot;<br>    req(inFile)<br>    <br>    f &lt;- read.csv(inFile$datapath, header = input$header, sep = input$sep, quote = input$quote)<br>    vars &lt;- names(dulieu)<br>    # Update select input<br>    updateSelectInput(session, &quot;columns&quot;,&quot;Select Columns&quot;, choices = vars)<br>    <br>    f<br>  })<br>  <br>  output$table_display &lt;- renderTable({<br>   <br>    f &lt;- dulieu()<br>    bienpt &lt;- subset(f, select = input$column) #subsetting <br>    <br>    #for cross validation <br>    cv &lt;- function(idp) {x_idw = gstat(id=&quot;bienpt&quot;, formula = bienpt~1,<br>                                         data = f, set = list(idp=idp))<br>.....................<br><br>My problem comes here. In the function(idp), bienpt is updated from the user&#39;s chosen. However, shiny give the error &quot;invalid type (list) for variable &quot;bienpt&quot;&quot;because bienpt is not available as a column name in data f (as I understood). <br><br>How can I use a selected column in this case? <br><br>Thank you so much for any advice! ;-0 <br><br>Best regards,  <br></div>"
